NEON I2_S prompt processing: 2x8 gemm tiles, constant-shift unpack, NEON quantize_row_i8_s

ggml_gemm_i2_i8_s on NEON now takes 2 weight rows x 8 activation columns per tile (each unpacked weight
vector feeds 8 sdots; no register spills), keeps the 4x4 tile for a last group of 4 columns, and unpacks
the bit-planes with constant shifts (the 0010 version shifted by a variable, which compiled to widening
instructions). The I2_S mul_mat path in ggml-cpu.c passes 8 columns per call on NEON (4 elsewhere, so
x86 is unchanged). quantize_row_i8_s gets a NEON loop with bit-identical results (vrndaq_f32 rounds like
roundf, saturating narrows clamp). On an M1 Max, single core: gemm 75 -> 150 GMAC/s; quantize 5.6x;
2B-4T pp512 at 8 threads 220.6 -> 387.0 t/s.

